# HomePi Global Cursor Rules

## Purpose

These rules define the global architectural standards for the HomePi platform.

HomePi is a modular, event-driven home automation platform designed for:
- Raspberry Pi
- long-running daemon services
- real-time communication
- AI-assisted development
- deterministic runtime behavior
- production-grade reliability
- git hub repository: https://github.com/nspinelli/homepi

These rules MUST be followed by all generated code.

---

# Core Architectural Philosophy

## Contracts First

All systems MUST be driven by:
- documented contracts
- schemas
- structured messages
- deterministic runtime behavior

Do not invent undocumented behavior.

---

## Event-Driven First

HomePi prefers:
- events
- interrupts
- subscriptions
- snapshots + deltas

Avoid polling whenever possible.

Polling is only acceptable when:
- hardware requires it
- external systems require it
- explicitly documented

---

## AI-Readable Architecture

The codebase must remain:
- predictable
- traceable
- observable
- schema-driven
- highly structured

AI agents must be able to:
- reconstruct runtime behavior
- trace failures
- identify ownership
- follow message flow
- determine authoritative state

---

